{#- SEVEN SERVICES, ARRANGED AROUND A CENTRE.

    Seven never sat right in a three-column grid — two full rows and a lone
    card stranded on the third. Seven around a circle is exactly even:
    360 / 7 = 51.4286 degrees apart.

    The radial placement is purely presentational (CSS transforms keyed off
    :nth-child), so this stays an ordinary list of links: DOM order is reading
    order is tab order. Below 940px it collapses to a single column, because a
    circle of seven panels at phone width is unreadable.

    THE ORB CARRIES A STAND-IN MARK. When Kevin supplies a real logo file,
    replace the contents of .orb__mark with the image and nothing else here
    needs to change. -#}
<div class="orb-field">

  <div class="orb-halo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="orb-track" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="orb" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="orb__core">
      <b class="orb__mark">TPS</b>
      <span class="orb__sub">Ferndown &middot; Dorset</span>
    </span>
  </div>

  <ul class="orb-panels">
    {%- for s in tps.services %}
    <li class="orb-panel">
      <a class="orb-link" href="{{ s.url }}">
        <span class="orb-link__media">
          {% image s.image, "", "200px" %}
        </span>
        <span class="orb-link__name">{{ s.shortName or s.name }}</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>

</div>
